=== SURVEY ===
Surveyed: useFSM.ts hooks (useFSMStats, useFSMTransitions), FSM types (FSMStats, FSMTransition,
FSMTransitionResponse), WidgetShell props, registry.ts structure, StateTimelineWidget (pattern ref),
SleepEfficiencyWidget (pattern ref), charts barrel (PieChart, Pie, Cell, Tooltip, ResponsiveContainer),
EmptyState component, numberFormat (fmtNumber, fmtInt), dateFormat (formatRelative).

FSMStats shape: { enabled: boolean, stats: Record<string, number>, active_subs?: ActiveSubFSM[] }
  - stats maps state name → milliseconds in state
FSMTransitionResponse shape: { data: FSMTransition[], total, page, per_page }
  - FSMTransition: { id, vehicle_id, fsm_type, from_state, to_state, trigger, guard, mode, duration_in_state_ms, created_at }

No unit-conversion needed — FSM data is state names and durations (ms), no physical units.

=== REASONING ===
Standard (2×4):
  - Donut chart via PieChart + Pie (innerRadius=55%) showing time distribution by state
  - Legend below chart: colored dots + state name + percentage
  - Below: last 5 transitions feed (from→to badge, relative timestamp)
  - Colors: driving=cyan, charging=green, asleep=purple, idle=amber, offline=gray

Compact (1×2):
  - Current state badge (highest time state as dominant) + time in current state
  - No chart (too small), centered layout

Freshness: merged from both statsQuery + transitionsQuery (max dataUpdatedAt).
Null safety: stats ?? {}, data ?? [], value ?? 0, label ?? '—'.
All strings via t() with 'dashboard' namespace.

